# ${feature}

User task: ${purpose}

Owner: `trip/Features/${feature}`. Follow `${feature}RootView` →
`${feature}Controller` → `${feature}Model`. The starter only renders injected
content; implement this task before connecting it to a product entry point.

## Implementation contract

- Start with `python3 scripts/workspace.py context ${feature} --json`.
- Define the observable benefit and acceptance cases in [a task brief](../../templates/task.md).
- Models own state and behavior; controllers store only their model.
- Inject external services and host callbacks through model initializers.
- Use TripDomain for shared values and service contracts. No sibling state access.
- Add localized content, loading/empty/failure states, cancellation, and local previews.
- App owns navigation and composition; connect through an existing contextual entry point.
- Record persistence, identity, accessibility, and async behavior before review.

## Integration checklist

- State the existing entry point and the specific App composition file that will own this model.
- Keep live service creation in `trip/App/Dependencies`; previews supply local services.
- List domain values/contracts to reuse; record any new package edge in the ownership manifest.
- Identify the lifetime of drafts, selections, pending requests, and stored values.
- Exercise success, empty, failure/retry, cancellation, long content, and accessible layouts.
- Confirm cancel preserves saved data, repeated actions are safe, and stale results cannot replace current state.
- Add the contextual entry point only after the interaction and recovery behavior work.

## Verification

Run `bash scripts/check.sh`. The ownership entry is already registered.
Run builds and benchmarks only when requested. Report source, compilation, and
runtime/visual evidence separately, including what remains unverified.
Use [future test seams](../Testing.md) for later coverage and service fakes.
